 keep this competitive, so a modest Democratic edge with wide uncertainty is warranted.", "watch": "GOP super PAC spending is ramping up against Brown; if it closes the polling gap by late October, this moves back toward a pure tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Appointed Senator Jon Husted faces former Senator Sherrod Brown in Ohio's special Senate election, one of the cycle's most expensive and closely watched contests. Brown has led in nearly every public poll since mid-August, with recent surveys from Marist, Suffolk, and even Republican-leaning firms showing him ahead by three to eight points. Ratings are split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets give Brown roughly a 60 percent chance.\n\nHusted benefits from Ohio's Republican-leaning electorate and heavy outside spending from Senate Leadership Fund, while Brown counters with a substantial fundraising and cash-on-hand advantage and a working-class appeal that has historically overperformed in the state. The race remains genuinely competitive, but the weight of recent evidence points to a narrow Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7432, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7463, "margin": 3.0}]}